Future of Cyber Law:
  Hosted by Pavan Duggal, this seminar talks about the changing nature of cyberlaw since the creation of the internet, and the potential changes that still need to be
  made. Here are some notes taken from the seminar:
  Utah was the first state to create cyber law
  Current cyber law encapsulates almost everything to do with online/ digital activities
  The increase in cyber terrorism required much stronger international co-operation
  The quantity of cyber breaches kept increasing month-to-month, and cybersecurity became very importants for stakeholders and companies
  At the time of the video, there was no one agreement on what constitutes internet restrictions
  Expected that by 2020, 20 billion devices will be connected to the internet
